Z||000001||Trixi||03-05-2000||09:56 AM||||What else is a tach filter called?  It's got to have another name!  <P>Does the Haynes manual makereference to it?  I know it doesn't under tach filter, but another name???<P>Help!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000002||FIERONUT||03-05-2000||11:14 AM||||I didnt see it mentioned in the Haynes...It is referred to as the tachometer filter.I found it in the original fiero manual.I did eventually find mine.Havent repaired it yet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-06-2000||09:05 PM||||   Yo, Nut, What are the symptoms that you are experiencing with your tach that leads you to believe your tach filter might be bad. The reason I ask is, I was having trouble with my tach jumping around. I thought about replacing the tach filter until I completed my plug and plug-wire exchange. problem gone. probably just interference. Worth a shot if this is your symptom.   ||||reg||10
Z||000004||sluppy123||03-07-2000||06:06 PM||||I agree with BAM-BAM, I also had what I believed to be a failed tach filter, I swapped it with the one from my other GT and it still jumped around. The Cap, Rotor, Plugs, Wires. were all replaced and the Tach worked great.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000005||Capt Fiero||03-07-2000||06:11 PM||||It can also be a poor coil.  A friend had his die on the last club run.  He had been complaing about his tach being jumpy but ignored it.  When we installed a new coil his tach fixed itself.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FIERONUT||03-08-2000||12:21 AM||||WELL...I replaced the ignition module plugs rotor distributor.....did a check on the ignition coil..and still the tach is still jumpin...i disconnected it for now...it was driving me crazy,,,,my mechanic did change sum wires but still did not work...so im stuck now...my last resort is 2 change the tach filter..the car also spurts and while driving at a steady speed it surges forward..i give up.....mechanic says it may be a grounding problem or even a vacuum leak...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Capt Fiero||03-08-2000||01:46 AM||||Borrow a spare coil from someone, I will almost bet, that will fix your car. You did not mention the spurts at steady speed.  When you get bouncing and spurts at the same time that means that you do not have enough juice.  (yes that was a joke too) but please before you go and spend a ton of money.  Install a coil from someone else and try it.  Hell if you want to pay shipping I will send you a near new coil to test with.<BR>David  email me, so that I am sure to get the message.  <BR>David||||reg||1
